{"step_index":266,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:48:22Z","content":"To push your completed StreamWave project to GitHub (which will automatically trigger your Vercel deployment), open your terminal or command prompt in your project folder and run the following commands:\n\n### 🐙 GitHub & Vercel Deployment Commands\n\n```bash\n# 1. Stage all updated project files\ngit add .\n\n# 2. Commit the changes with a clear commit message\ngit commit -m \"feat: Add StreamWave landing page, simulated checkout, signed cookie access control, and logo watermark\"\n\n# 3. Push to your main branch on GitHub (triggers Vercel auto-deploy)\ngit push origin main\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🎉 Summary of Completed Features\n\n- 🍿 **5-Second MP4 Video Preview**: Added `public/media/streamwave-preview.mp4` with a dedicated HTML5 video modal player for all movie cards.\n- 🎨 **StreamWave Visual Identity**: Resized brand logo (`/images/streamwave-logo.png`), applied custom favicons, and configured action buttons (\"▶ Watch\" for movies / \"▶ Play\" for music).\n- 🌐 **Public Landing Page (`/`)**: Full-height hero section with Zimbabwean streaming messaging, email registration form, benefits grid, how-it-works workflow, supported payment badges, and a StreamWave background watermark.\n- 💳 **Academic Payment Simulation (`/checkout`)**: Interactive EcoCash (`077 000 0000`), Visa (`4242`), and MasterCard (`4444`) checkout options featuring visual step progress animations, simulated approval (`SW-DEMO-XXXXX` ref), and simulated decline testing.\n- 🔐 **Signed Cookie Access Control**: Enforces HMAC-SHA256 signed HTTP-only `streamwave_session` cookies to protect `/library` and backend media endpoints (`/api/media`).\n- 🛡️ **Security & Academic Audit**: Zero financial APIs contacted, zero sensitive card credentials transmitted/stored, sanitized structured telemetry logging, and full security disclaimer added to `README.md`.\n- 🧪 **100% Automated Test Coverage**: Comprehensive Pytest suite in `tests/test_api.py`."}
