{"step_index":270,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T20:20:38Z","content":"That error means Git hasn't been initialized in this directory yet. \n\nHere is how to push depending on your setup:\n\n---\n\n### Option A: If you already have a cloned GitHub folder on your computer\nNavigate to the folder where you originally cloned your StreamWave repository from GitHub (e.g. on your Desktop or Projects folder), for example:\n\n```cmd\ncd C:\\Users\\dell\\Desktop\\your-streamwave-repo-name\n```\n*(Replace with your actual GitHub folder path)*\n\nThen run:\n```cmd\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"feat: Add StreamWave landing page, simulated checkout, signed cookie access control, and logo watermark\"\ngit push origin main\n```\n\n---\n\n### Option B: If you want to connect this current folder to a new or existing GitHub repository\n\nRun these commands step-by-step:\n\n1. **Initialize Git in this folder**:\n   ```cmd\n   git init\n   ```\n\n2. **Stage all files and commit**:\n   ```cmd\n   git add .\n   git commit -m \"feat: Add StreamWave landing page, simulated checkout, signed cookie access control, and logo watermark\"\n   ```\n\n3. **Set main branch name**:\n   ```cmd\n   git branch -M main\n   ```\n\n4. **Connect to your GitHub repository**:\n   *(Replace `https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/YOUR_REPO.git` with your actual GitHub repository URL)*\n   ```cmd\n   git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/YOUR_REPO.git\n   ```\n\n5. **Push to GitHub**:\n   ```cmd\n   git push -u origin main\n   ```"}
